{
  "_read_first": "Follow agent/updating.md with this manifest pinned to main's commit, or to the full commit the request names (on main or not, tagged or not). The deployment map uses the tool recorded in status; the harness's installed-file receipt (status/installed-files.json) decides which files are Orion's, and update/pristine.json only migrates a harness without one. The request is consent: never stop to ask, and never replace a file the client has changed: a changed runtime or plugin file, or plugin catalog, stops the update instead.",
  "_what": "deployment is the source-to-destination and ownership contract for separate client repositories; select exactly one recorded tool. 2.0.0 is a reinstall release: this manifest updates 2.0.0 and later only (agent/reinstall-from-1.x.md). Contract: agent/updating.md and deployment._contract.",
  "_regenerate": "Map every file under plugins/orion/ in deployment.entries, once each, with no per-tool destinations: the package ships at its own path for every tool. update/pristine.json is frozen compatibility data: never regenerate it; the release contract validates it.",
  "template_version": "2.0.0",
  "never_touch": {
    "status/status.json": "The client's own record: preserve pairing, setup checkpoint, stages, packages and choices. An update edits template_version and appends one notes line. node status/send.mjs migrate may add the default send level. The shared guard updates sharing.pairing at runtime; it never resets a recorded clock. Setup may persist its own checkpoint. These runtime state changes do not authorize replacing the client's status file.",
    "status/send-log.md": "the client's own record of every send decision and verdict, content-free (since 1.5.0)",
    "status/no-contact.md": "the client's own no-contact list, for good (since 1.5.0)",
    "status/waiting.md": "the client's list of messages waiting for them, rewritten by every run (since 1.5.0)",
    "status/shift-log.md": "the client's work history",
    "status/work-log.md": "the client's work history: one line per finished task they asked for (since 1.1.0)",
    "status/shifts/": "legacy wake-up files and schedule records specific to the original computer and folder",
    "agent/knowledge-base/01..07*.md": "the client's business, captured in their words",
    ".claude/agents/ (everything but nothing — the whole directory)": "the client's hired team; the roster README carries their rows",
    ".claude/skills/ and .agents/skills/ (every skill there)": "skills the client taught or added; Orion’s shipped skills live in plugins/orion/",
    ".update-backup/": "prior updates' safety copies",
    "status/radio-outbox.json": "Client-owned durable labels-only pending reports; never replace, retire or discard on update.",
    "status/.radio-lock/": "Client-owned cross-process runtime lock; recovery must establish that its owner has stopped before removal.",
    "status/radio.key": "Machine-local credential; never print, refresh, retire, or save to the home repository.",
    "status/installed-files.json": "This harness's installed-file receipt: the Orion-managed files actually installed and their fingerprints. Harness-owned ownership evidence, written by Orion's installer and updater only; never replaced from a release.",
    "anything outside the deployment map": "an update writes only the destinations the deployment map plans for the recorded tool, and retires only listed retired entries; nothing else may be touched"
  },
